\tag{fdip}
\title{A Clifford algebra before a metric}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{The endomorphism ring of an exterior algebra carries one
Clifford algebra before any quadratic form is chosen. A
bilinear form selects a graph inside that algebra. The derived
form of \ref{fdip-00PB} and the twisted form of
\ref{fdip-00Q1} are two such graphs. Which standard identities
survive without a recovery site, and which do not?}

